KG42.register("clusters-7ae5edaa5405984cb967c95a",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v142-d-CL005","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","label":"Price-based local dispatch benchmark with no requirement to submit demand bids","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL005","label":"Price-based local dispatch benchmark with no requirement to submit demand bids","market_meaning":"Under the price-based benchmark, the microgrid has no obligation to submit demand bids; the controller uses price signals to perform local least-cost dispatch and determine main-grid exchange. The ISO provides the background through load-forecast-based clearing and price pass-through, and the correspondence between forecast prices and actual LMP remains to be clarified.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Only the M02 benchmark is assembled. The forecast day-ahead price, the LMP after ISO clearing, and the separately described DMO pricing numerical scenario have no clear correspondence yet and are retained separately; the absence of a bidding requirement does not mean that electricity trading is prohibited, nor does it transfer the bidding allocation or deviation charge mathematics from M01.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The absence of a bidding obligation and local cost decisions after price input jointly define the price-based mechanism, distinct from deviation policy after quantity allocation. The interaction between load and LMP is retained as an intra-chain result or risk description, and no price-iteration loop is created on that basis.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"This provides an exemption from the demand-bid submission obligation under the benchmark as a mechanism-scope condition for local price dispatch."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"This provides the price input, the microgrid's local dispatch responsibility, and the ISO forecast-clearing background; the price timing and entity differences within the same chain continue to be retained."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E06"],"rationale":"The citation for the same mechanism explicitly juxtaposes the absence of a microgrid bidding requirement and the determination of main-grid exchange by local cost minimization, supporting the composition of the price-based benchmark; this is a complementarity of mechanism scope and does not add a causal edge from the bidding exemption to a dispatch result."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G015","category":"unverified_source","description":"All citations for the price-based benchmark remain unverified candidates; no independent source audit or downstream scientific review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g02-E25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent checks should verify the benchmark definition, the timing of price information, and the scope of the numerical example, while retaining the current candidate status and uncertainty."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G016","category":"math_incomplete","description":"At present there is only a procedural description of price-based local least-cost dispatch, and it lacks the objective, constraints, and typed objects for DER, load, main-grid exchange, and price under the same mechanism. Empty mathematical fields are a limitation of the existing graph and must not be interpreted as these quantities not existing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R012::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B/C are to extract the M02-specific objective, constraints, variables, and price definition; when there is no explicit source, the procedural description is to be maintained, without filling it in with M01 variables or formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G017","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R012 simultaneously records descriptions of the forecast day-ahead price, the actual post-clearing price, and the ISO-determined LMP; the same mechanism also has a numerical scenario receiving DMO pricing, and it has not yet been explained whether these prices are the same or how they correspond by stage or case.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C004","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g02-E25","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g03-e06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the entities, timing, and case conditions of the price forecast, ISO formation, utility pass-through, and DMO pricing scenario, and then decide whether there is the same price object or different branches; at present, no cross-price same-quantity mapping is established."}]},"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R011","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R012"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-3ec465666397863a"]});
